# .dockerignore - keep non-application content out of the deployed image.
#
# Dockerfile does `COPY . /var/www/html`, so without this file a local build
# ships the developer's .env (APP_KEY, client secret, DB password), the whole
# .git history, database backups and logs into the image. On Railway the build
# context is the git checkout so most of these are absent already, but a local
# `docker build` would bake them in. Excluding them is free and removes a
# credential-leak path.

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- VCS / tooling ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.workbuddy-ai/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Runtime data (may contain user data or credentials) -------------------
storage/backups/
storage/logs/*
!storage/logs/.gitkeep
*.log
*.sql.gz
*dump*.sql

# --- Python AI service build artefacts -------------------------------------
ai-service/venv/
ai-service/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- OS / editor junk ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__MACOSX/
._*

# --- Docs (not needed at runtime) ------------------------------------------
README.md
README-RECONCILIATION.md
sdc-frame-prompt.md
